{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.1.14", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.1.14"}, "paraphrase": "I bow to Kṛṣṇa, who is fivefold: in the form of a devotee (Caitanya), the expansion of a devotee (Nityānanda), the incarnation of a devotee (Advaita), the pure devotee (Śrīvāsa) and the energy of a devotee (Gadādhara).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:panca-tattva"], "terms": ["trm:panca-tattva"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.1.3", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.1.3"}, "paraphrase": "What the Upaniṣads call the non-dual Brahman is the effulgence of his body; the indwelling Self (Paramātman) is his partial expansion; the Bhagavān full of six opulences is he himself — there is no truth higher than Kṛṣṇa Caitanya.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:brahman-paramatman-bhagavan"], "notes": "Verse also repeated at CC 1.2.5.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.1.45-47", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.1.45-47"}, "paraphrase": "According to scripture the guru is a form of Kṛṣṇa; in the form of the guru Kṛṣṇa shows mercy to devotees. The instructing guru is known as Kṛṣṇa's own form in two ways: as the indwelling Lord and as the best of devotees.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-in-gaudiya"], "terms": ["trm:siksa-guru", "trm:caitya-guru"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.1.5", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.1.5"}, "paraphrase": "Rādhā is the transformation of Kṛṣṇa's love, his pleasure-giving power (hlādinī); though one in self, they took two bodies of old; now the two have become one again as Caitanya — I bow to him, Kṛṣṇa himself, enriched with Rādhā's emotion and lustre.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:svarupa-damodara"], "concepts": ["cpt:caitanya-as-radha-krsna", "cpt:radha-hladini-sakti"], "terms": ["trm:hladini"], "notes": "Attributed to Svarūpa Dāmodara's notebook.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.1.6", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.1.6"}, "paraphrase": "Desiring to know the greatness of Rādhā's love, the wondrous sweetness of his own that she relishes, and the happiness she feels in realising him, the moon Hari took birth, rich with her emotion, from the ocean of Śacī's womb.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:svarupa-damodara"], "concepts": ["cpt:caitanya-as-radha-krsna"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.17.21", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.17.21"}, "paraphrase": "(Quoting the Bṛhannāradīya Purāṇa:) the name of Hari, the name of Hari, the name of Hari alone — in the Kali age there is no other way, no other way, no other way.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "harer nāma harer nāma harer nāmaiva kevalam | kalau nāsty eva nāsty eva nāsty eva gatir anyathā ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:kali-yuga-dharma"], "practices": ["prc:nama-sankirtana"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.17.31", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.17.31"}, "paraphrase": "Caitanya's verse on the humility with which to chant (Śikṣāṣṭaka 3) is quoted: humbler than grass, more tolerant than a tree, respecting others without seeking respect, one should always sing Hari's name.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "cross_refs": ["tea:siksastaka:3"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.17/2", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.17"}, "paraphrase": "When the Kazi of Navadvīpa banned the chanting, Caitanya led a great procession of kīrtana to his house; the Kazi, after conversation, allowed the chanting to continue (tradition's account).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "practices": ["prc:nama-sankirtana"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.4.165", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.4.165"}, "paraphrase": "The desire to please one's own senses is called lust (kāma); the desire to please Kṛṣṇa's senses is called love (prema).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics", "consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "obstacles": ["obs:kama"], "terms": ["trm:prema"], "concepts": ["cpt:parakiya-svakiya"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.4.68", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.4.68"}, "paraphrase": "The essence of the pleasure power (hlādinī) is love; the essence of love is emotion (bhāva); the utmost limit of emotion is called great emotion (mahābhāva) — Rādhā.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:radha-hladini-sakti", "cpt:hladini-sandhini-samvit"], "terms": ["trm:mahabhava"], "notes": "Verse number to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:1.7", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "1.7"}, "paraphrase": "At Kāśī Caitanya answers Prakāśānanda and the Advaita renouncers: the Brahma Sūtras teach transformation (pariṇāma) of the Lord's power, not unreal appearance; the Lord, like the touchstone that produces gold, remains unchanged while the world arises; the great saying is the syllable Oṃ, not 'that thou art'; Śaṅkara abandoned the direct sense of scripture for a secondary one; love of Kṛṣṇa (prema) is the fifth and highest human aim.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya", "tch:prakasananda-sarasvati"], "concepts": ["cpt:sakti-parinama", "cpt:prema-as-fifth-goal"], "disputes": ["dsp:gaudiya-critique-of-advaita", "dsp:brahma-parinama-vada", "dsp:prema-beyond-moksa"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference (CC 1.7, c. vv. 100–150); specific verses (e.g. 1.7.121–130) to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.19.149", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.19.149"}, "paraphrase": "The devotee of Kṛṣṇa is desireless and therefore peaceful; those who desire enjoyment, liberation or perfections (siddhi) are all restless.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:devotee-rejects-siddhis"], "obstacles": ["obs:bhukti-mukti-sprha"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.19.151", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.19.151"}, "paraphrase": "Wandering through the universe, some fortunate soul, by the grace of guru and Kṛṣṇa, receives the seed of the creeper of devotion.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "beginner", "stage_native": "bhakti-latā-bīja"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "brahmāṇḍa bhramite kona bhāgyavān jīva | guru-kṛṣṇa-prasāde pāya bhakti-latā-bīja ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "notes": "Bengali verse.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.20-24", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.20-24"}, "paraphrase": "Caitanya's instruction to Sanātana at Vārāṇasī: the relation (sambandha: Kṛṣṇa, his powers, avatāras and abodes), the means (abhidheya: devotion, rule-based and spontaneous) and the goal (prayojana: love), including the sixty-one meanings of the ātmārāma verse.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:sambandha-abhidheya-prayojana"], "notes": "Chapter-range reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.20.108", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.20.108"}, "paraphrase": "The soul's constitutional nature is to be an eternal servant of Kṛṣṇa; it is Kṛṣṇa's marginal power, a manifestation simultaneously one with and different from him.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "jīvera 'svarūpa' haya — kṛṣṇera 'nitya-dāsa' | kṛṣṇera 'taṭasthā-śakti' 'bhedābheda-prakāśa' ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:jiva-as-tatastha-sakti", "cpt:acintya-bhedabheda"], "terms": ["trm:tatastha-sakti", "trm:nitya-dasa"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.22.128", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.22.128"}, "paraphrase": "Associating with saints, chanting the name, hearing the Bhāgavata, living in Mathurā and serving the deity with faith — (these five are the most potent limbs of devotion).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "sound", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "practices": ["prc:five-potent-limbs"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.22.78-80", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.22.78-80"}, "paraphrase": "The twenty-six qualities of a Vaiṣṇava are listed: kind, non-injurious, truthful, equal to all, faultless, generous, mild, clean, without possessions, helpful to all, peaceful, taking refuge only in Kṛṣṇa, desireless, without worldly endeavour, steady, victorious over the six enemies, moderate in eating, sane, respectful, without pride, grave, compassionate, friendly, poetic, expert and silent.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:twenty-six-qualities-of-a-vaisnava"], "notes": "Verse range approximate.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.6", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.6"}, "paraphrase": "At Purī, the Advaita teacher Sārvabhauma expounds Śaṅkara's reading of the Vedānta for seven days; Caitanya replies that the sūtras and Upaniṣads speak directly of the personal Lord with transcendental qualities, criticises the impersonalist commentary, explains the ātmārāma verse (BhP 1.7.10) in many ways, and Sārvabhauma becomes his devotee.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya", "tch:sarvabhauma-bhattacarya"], "disputes": ["dsp:gaudiya-critique-of-advaita", "dsp:saguna-nirguna", "dsp:advaita-crypto-buddhism"], "notes": "Chapter-level. In this chapter Caitanya is also reported to say that atheism relying on the Veda is worse than Buddhism (verse c. 2.6.168, to verify).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.8", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.8"}, "paraphrase": "In the dialogue with Rāmānanda Rāya, Caitanya asks for the goal and means; each answer — duties of class and stage, offering works to Kṛṣṇa, giving up one's duty, devotion mixed with knowledge — is called 'external, go further', until devotion free of knowledge, love, and then love in servitude, friendship, parental affection and conjugal love, rising to Rādhā's love and the love-play of the divine couple, are accepted.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "action", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya", "tch:ramananda-raya"], "paths": ["pth:ramananda-samvada-ladder"], "concepts": ["cpt:five-devotional-rasas"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference (CC 2.8, c. vv. 57–200).", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:2.8.128", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "2.8.128"}, "paraphrase": "Whether a brāhmaṇa, a renunciant or a śūdra — whoever knows the truth about Kṛṣṇa is a guru.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "ethics"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:guru-in-gaudiya"], "disputes": ["dsp:women-caste-liberation"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:3.11", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "3.11"}, "paraphrase": "Haridāsa Ṭhākura passes away at Purī with Caitanya's name on his lips and Caitanya's form before his eyes; Caitanya dances with his body in kīrtana, buries him by the sea and begs food for a festival in his honour.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["death-dying"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja"], "concepts": ["cpt:last-thought"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:3.14-20", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "3.14-20"}, "paraphrase": "In his last years at Purī, Caitanya lives in Rādhā's separation from Kṛṣṇa: states of inner absorption, half-external and external consciousness alternate; he utters the words of divine madness (divyonmāda), and at the end recites the Śikṣāṣṭaka.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "consciousness-mind"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:caitanya"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-dasas-of-caitanya", "cpt:viraha-bhakti"], "terms": ["trm:divyonmada"], "notes": "Chapter-range reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:caitanya-caritamrta:3.3", "source": "src:caitanya-caritamrta", "location": {"ref": "3.3"}, "paraphrase": "Haridāsa Ṭhākura teaches in an assembly that even a semblance of the name (nāmābhāsa), uttered without full intent, destroys sins and gives liberation, as the rising sun's first glow dispels darkness; pure chanting of the name gives love.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["sound-language", "karma-liberation"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:krsnadasa-kaviraja", "tch:haridasa-thakura"], "concepts": ["cpt:namabhasa"], "terms": ["trm:namabhasa"], "cross_refs": ["tea:bhagavata-purana:6.1-2"], "notes": "Chapter-level reference.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
